From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: glacier <hyouga.dev@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 24 Aug 2026 08:55:07 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] Use the shared enum arrays on the per-tick paths

Enum.values() clones its backing array on every call. EnumDirection.VALUES already existed
for this reason but twenty call sites still used values(), among them the neighbour scans
in redstone wire, redstone torch, repeaters, pistons, fire and liquids - all of which run
inside block ticks.

EnumCreatureType gets the same treatment: Chunk.a and Chunk.b walked values() on every
entity that entered or left a chunk. Nothing writes to either array.

The remaining values() calls are in static initialisers sizing lookup tables, where the
copy happens once and the ordering hazard of touching VALUES during class init is real.

